00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
“Follow your instincts.” 

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
I heard the voice of Nunyati in my head. 

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
“When time will come, you’ll realise that you know where to go.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Your ancestors have followed that path before you, it’s all there, in your DNA. Just listen to their voice. They will guide you.” 

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Back then, I remember listening to him in total disbelief. 

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:55.000
How could I ever know my way in total darkness, without a map, without someone to show me the way? 

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:07.000
I envied the sparrows, the geese, who travelled in flocks, following the older, more experienced migrants. I was alone. 

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:20.000
And yet, he was right. I realised I knew the way. Without a doubt, I trusted my ancestors’ heritage, and I flew, as fast as the wind. 

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
How could I ever describe that feeling? That sense of total freedom? That sensation that you are finally meeting your destiny? 

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.000
It was exhilarating. I felt invincible. 

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:43.000
I was racing into the night, further and faster than I had ever gone. Me who had never flown more than a few miles! 

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
I saw the men’s lights beneath me, those little electric lines of roads and villages, like a spiderweb. 

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:57.000
They looked so small, so frail. You can’t catch me now, I laughed. 

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:08.000
And then, suddenly, the spiderweb stopped. There was just total darkness. A world of shadows. 

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.000
My heart started racing, so I decided to land on a tree at the limit of the men’s kingdom to rest. 

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.000
The sun was rising at the horizon. And then, I saw it.  

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Ahead of me lay an area of unimaginable emptiness. An immense stretch of land that humans had been too terrified to conquer. 

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:42.000
And here I was, a little bird, knowing that my destiny was beneath it. 

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:53.000
The world’s greatest desert. The Sahara. 
